From 33b4c370f7de02844490c3978c72ac44f24f5609 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xinyue Ling <xinyling@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 10:25:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix wrong current_mode selection for 6 GHz ACS result

When ACS completes on a 6 GHz channel (e.g., iface->freq=6295 MHz),
hostapd_acs_channel_selected() selects current_mode by iterating
hw_features and skipping modes whose type matches acs_res->hw_mode
but that do not contain iface->freq. The skip check previously used
hw_get_chan(), which searches all hw_features entries of the given
mode type rather than the specific mode instance under test. Since
both 5 GHz and 6 GHz report HOSTAPD_MODE_IEEE80211A, searching all
hw_features for freq=6295 MHz finds it in the 6 GHz entry, causing
the 5 GHz mode to NOT be skipped. The loop therefore terminates with
current_mode pointing to the 5 GHz hw_features entry instead of the
6 GHz one.

Subsequent DFS processing then operates on the 5 GHz channel table
with a 6 GHz channel number, producing "DFS chan_idx seems wrong".

To fix this, replace hw_get_chan() with hw_mode_get_channel(), which
limits the frequency search to the specific mode instance being
evaluated, correctly skipping the 5 GHz entry when iface->freq is a
6 GHz frequency.

Signed-off-by: Xinyue Ling <xinyling@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/ap/drv_callbacks.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
index 1d85d97..5dd04de 100644
--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -1529,10 +1529,9 @@ void hostapd_acs_channel_selected(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 
 			if (mode->mode == acs_res->hw_mode) {
 				if (hapd->iface->freq > 0 &&
-				    !hw_get_chan(mode->mode,
-						 hapd->iface->freq,
-						 hapd->iface->hw_features,
-						 hapd->iface->num_hw_features))
+				    !hw_mode_get_channel(mode,
+							 hapd->iface->freq,
+							 NULL))
 					continue;
 				hapd->iface->current_mode = mode;
 				break;
